  "rules": [
    "When recent history shows a strong downtrend (e.g., Example 1), the model systematically overestimates future prices by ignoring immediate volatility and mean reversion; apply a downward bias correction of -5% to -10% on the forecasted path.",
    "When sentiment is mixed or negative in the last 3 days, the model fails to capture sudden upward spikes (e.g., Examples 2-5); reduce the initial forecast step size by 15-20% and flatten the curve to account for volatility clustering.",
    "The model exhibits a 'smoothness bias' where it predicts linear growth after volatile periods; correct this by introducing random walk variance equal to the standard deviation of the last 5 days into every forecast step.",
    "In scenarios with high sentiment noise (values >0.25), the model's long-term horizon is overly optimistic; apply a mean-reversion floor at the average of the last 10 days for the first 7 forecast steps.",
    "When history ends near a local peak followed by negative sentiment, the model fails to predict an immediate drop; reverse the forecast direction immediately if the last 3 data points show a downward slope."
  ]
}
